WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.663
- And then, I'll go,

00:00:03.808 --> 00:00:04.785
Coming at ya!

00:00:04.785 --> 00:00:07.118
(screaming)

00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:12.989
(light piano music)

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.860
The house in this street was

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.680
the first house that we were in,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.190
me, my mom, and my sister.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.023
(dog barking)

00:00:21.023 --> 00:00:23.440
I was just kind of did
everything everyone else did.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.420
Like, I like, I don't know

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.690
Like, I played on Nintendo or whatever.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.990
Or like, had a, yeah, Game Boy.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.560
Like, went through different obsessions.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.930
I liked to skateboard along here.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.110
Like, but, yeah.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:37.943
That was it.

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:39.620
Growing up in Crawley is,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.453
yeah.

00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:41.310
The same as anywhere else,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.143
I think so.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.019
- [Nichola] Oh, she was
a beautiful little kid.

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:54.040
- [Erin] What do you mean? I
thought I looked like a boy.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.420
- Well, you did look like a boy.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.777
In fact, everyone used to say,

00:00:57.777 --> 00:00:59.798
"What a beautiful little boy you have."

00:00:59.798 --> 00:01:00.631
- [Erin] Yeah.

00:01:00.631 --> 00:01:03.150
- [Nichola] When she was kind of younger,

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.010
she didn't have huge amounts of friends,

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:06.870
did you really?

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.060
- No.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:08.893
Oh no, no coasters.

00:01:08.893 --> 00:01:11.120
- Tended to have just one friend

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.220
and that was Amy.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.053
- Yeah.

00:01:13.053 --> 00:01:14.960
- And that's where the
football came into play.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:15.793
- Yeah!

00:01:15.793 --> 00:01:18.970
This is where I played on this
pitch for the school team.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.700
Like, for years and years and years.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.240
It's making me feel a little bit anxious,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.110
I'm not going to lie.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.520
I don't know what it is.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.754
School is just, I don't know.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:31.600
I loved the bits that I
loved about it, like, sports

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.860
and stuff like that and drama.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.030
But coming back here just makes me feel

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.593
like I'm doing something wrong.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.050
Oh fuck!

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:40.950
I couldn't get it!

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.070
(football thumps)

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.820
(birds chirping)

00:02:01.491 --> 00:02:03.184
What's this? I'm still going!

00:02:03.184 --> 00:02:04.017
What's she doing?

00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:04.978
(man offscreen exclaims)

00:02:04.978 --> 00:02:05.913
(Erin screaming)

00:02:05.913 --> 00:02:07.009
(man offscreen laughing)

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:09.230
How many did I do?

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.606
- You were really good at football.

00:02:11.606 --> 00:02:12.439
- And I loved it.

00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:14.040
- And it was a hard decision, I guess,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.020
for you to make at that time.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.150
- It was 'cause dad was driving me to--

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.990
- All over the southeast.
- Like Brighton.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.823
- Yup.
- And then having to

00:02:20.823 --> 00:02:23.730
get back in time.
- In time for me, then

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.712
- To drop off
- To drop you off to

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.545
- East Grinstead.
- East Grinstead, yeah.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:28.180
- It was too much.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.260
- It really was.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:30.909
So, I think it was Dad.

00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:32.575
- Yeah
- He sort of said to you,

00:02:32.575 --> 00:02:34.210
"Erin you've got to decide,

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.043
really,
- Yeah.

00:02:35.043 --> 00:02:36.020
what you want to do."

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:39.040
- From when I was four
and my sister was six,

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.860
we would go on the weekends,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.760
it was a Sunday,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.730
to drama club.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.390
And yeah, we pretty much did that together

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.223
up until,

00:02:47.223 --> 00:02:49.090
I don't know, I feel like
she would've been like 16.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.610
So, it lasted a long time when it was

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:51.910
our thing that we did.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.120
It came a moment when she dropped away,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:54.953
and I was just like,

00:02:54.953 --> 00:02:57.880
Oh no, yeah, this is my thing!

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.350
And it just like,

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.250
yeah, right.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.500
(light rhythmic music)

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.100
I would have been 18 when

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.323
we went to Bosnia,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.120
which was with Guy Williams.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.640
Because there's this
theater festival called

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.440
the Mostar Youtube Theater Festival.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.230
He was like, "We're
going to create a piece

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.017
of theater and we're gonna take it there."

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.560
Teachers have the power to blooming change

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.410
your whole, like,

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.320
path in life

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.380
and I genuinely feel that he changed mine.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.013
This is Guy Williams.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.200
This.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.000
- We did a piece of work that
just kind of caught fire.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.370
And that led to, "Okay,
we could go actually,

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.887
we could go there and
we could do a piece."

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.430
And even then still to
2010 so the award's been

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.027
over 15 years, it was still,

00:03:52.027 --> 00:03:54.370
"Bosnia, why don't you come to Bosnia?".

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.203
- Yeah.

00:03:55.203 --> 00:03:56.670
- Dangerous, scary place to go.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.740
And they created this amazing, I mean,

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.933
honestly, I was watching
it with my wife last night.

00:04:03.122 --> 00:04:07.260
(drawn out string music)

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.580
- I knew how special of a
piece it was that we created,

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.770
but it wasn't until the flight home,

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.573
knowing what you were a part of,

00:04:16.873 --> 00:04:20.003
that kind of community of
people that wanna make stuff.

00:04:20.974 --> 00:04:23.540
It just had such huge impact on me.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.017
When you speak to people and they're like,

00:04:25.017 --> 00:04:27.030
"When did you wanna just do acting?"

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.217
and I'm like, "Well, it was kind of there.

00:04:29.217 --> 00:04:30.450
"As I was growing up",

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.620
but that moment on the plane
home from Bosnia always

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.510
really rings out in my
mind because it kind

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.961
of like fed my soul in a way that

00:04:39.961 --> 00:04:44.961
you can't unlearn how
that tastes. So, yeah,

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.500
Bosnia genuinely, genuinely made

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:51.140
me consciously go, "Okay, this is it now".

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.170
- You went for audition after audition.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.420
You paid 200 pounds a time
and she got knocked back.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.760
She got knocked back the whole time.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.550
And it got to the point
she saved her money

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.119
to go to um, London, was it?
- Yeah.

00:05:05.119 --> 00:05:07.300
- London, all these different places.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.940
And saved her money to do it,

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.410
and she just got knocked back.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.100
- Yeah, it was horrible.
- And I cried,

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.400
because I thought where
do we go from here?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.038
- I just didn't know what to do.

00:05:19.038 --> 00:05:20.910
- What they expected of you--
- Yeah.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.080
- How to be, what to say.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.350
But that's what GSA gave you.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.300
- So from training in Gilford,

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.200
- Yeah.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.420
to then getting into Bristol--

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.347
- And then it was Bristol.
- Yeah.

00:05:30.347 --> 00:05:34.380
I'd never been to Bristol
before my meeting.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.960
I remember falling in love with the place,

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.200
but then you kind of,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.100
'cause Bristol is Bristol,

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.610
but Clifton is Clifton.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.720
And then just staring at the building

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:42.790
that is the Bristol Old Vic

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:44.367
and being like,

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.440
"I don't know",

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.440
something just...

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.083
It felt really magical.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.080
I think I spent my whole first year,

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.340
particularly, probably the first week,

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.710
literally just beamin'.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.749
- Yeah. And I remember lovely you

00:05:58.749 --> 00:06:00.380
with your lovely little top knot!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.600
- It was embarrassing.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.566
- Top knot and big boots.

00:06:03.566 --> 00:06:04.399
- It was so, yeah

00:06:04.399 --> 00:06:05.232
- It was adorable.

00:06:05.232 --> 00:06:06.540
- It was so embarrassing.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:07.373
- It's adorable.

00:06:07.373 --> 00:06:09.000
- Stop showing photos!
- Now this,

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.120
this was in the middle year,

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.920
that was the middle year
touring show wasn't it,

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.070
- That's second year, yeah.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.270
- This is "Heresy of Love"
that, that I directed,

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.000
and Erin and there's Ryan.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:23.500
- Ryan McKen is , like,
one of my best friends,

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:26.940
like, he, I met him at Bristol
Old Vic Theater School,

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.160
and we kind of, yeah we
clicked really early on,

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:33.090
because we both kind of
recognized a similarity

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.740
in the way that we approached it.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:36.751
- [Whispers] 1, 2 3

00:06:36.751 --> 00:06:40.589
(It Came Upon a Midnight Clear)

00:06:40.589 --> 00:06:42.422
- [Singing] Clear, la.

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:45.888
(laughing)

00:06:45.888 --> 00:06:48.805
(fingers snapping)

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:54.857
- And the shield

00:06:54.857 --> 00:06:56.170
- Are we on that?

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.880
- Oh my gosh.
- You were the first ones...

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:58.780
- We created an award.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:01.500
- You were the first
ones to be awarded this.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:02.700
You can't be more than 100%

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.000
but if you could be more than 100%

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:04.833
they would be more than

00:07:04.833 --> 00:07:06.930
100%. I mean they came with that,

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:08.600
they developed that, they pushed that,

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.390
they took everything that
we could possibly offer them

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.570
and they,

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:12.730
they ran with it.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.020
Anyway, your shield's in there,

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.120
- Oh my days!
- And your swords are here.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.140
- No! Come on!

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.285
- No!

00:07:20.285 --> 00:07:21.118
- What did you do?

00:07:21.118 --> 00:07:22.253
There and then it's up there

00:07:22.253 --> 00:07:23.214
- And it always needed to flip it,

00:07:23.214 --> 00:07:24.047
- And there!

00:07:24.047 --> 00:07:25.870
I remember that one felt wicked!

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:26.703
- That's really cool,

00:07:26.703 --> 00:07:27.689
you haven't forgotten
- Yeah!

00:07:27.689 --> 00:07:31.356
(Dramatic Orchestral Music)

00:07:39.678 --> 00:07:41.307
(sword clacks)

00:07:41.307 --> 00:07:43.474
(yelling)

00:07:50.857 --> 00:07:51.796
I got you!

00:07:51.796 --> 00:07:53.840
(laughs)

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.950
Whilst we were still in our final year

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.860
of Bristol Old Vic Theater School,

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.670
all of us were eligible to go up

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.290
for these meetings for this
show that's being put on

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.417
at the Bristol Old Vic called "Pink Mist".

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.130
And it was, yeah,

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.570
it was kind of the best
step up into the industry

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:11.860
that we could have asked for,

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:14.100
because you've kind of got the comfort

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.880
of being in Bristol which
you've been in for a while,

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.740
but you're genuinely on a stage

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:22.130
for a professional theater
for the first time.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:24.640
And my character was particularly angry,

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:27.080
so I remember kind of
like hyping myself up

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:29.970
for every show, going and doing,
like, skipping on the stage

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.330
like, just listening to Eminem, yeah.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.540
I'd get my clothes, I'd get my hair done,

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:35.373
and then like,

00:08:35.373 --> 00:08:36.540
just completely getting rid of everything,

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.040
and just going into your character,

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:41.193
which I love, like, I love
letting it all drop away.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.760
And right now the
biggest thing I've learnt

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.730
is that the more your life doesn't revolve

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:51.150
around this singular thing,

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.730
that you've put so much
importance on, the better.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:54.890
Like, I think it's really healthy

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:56.300
to know what you want to do,

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.520
that's totally fine and admirable,

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:01.510
but the more you fill your life

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:03.450
by playing volleyball, playing football,

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.840
going to the pub for a drink,
or going to the cinema,

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:08.860
just, other things, you win,

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:09.960
because your like ahh!

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.810
Like, it stays as this hobby
that actually is your job,

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.798
the more you fill your
life out with other things.

00:09:15.798 --> 00:09:17.240
- And, to see where you are now,

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.470
it's just incredible,

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.490
it's just,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:22.818
you know, I pick up a
newspaper, you're in it!

00:09:22.818 --> 00:09:23.837
(laughs)

00:09:23.837 --> 00:09:25.820
- It's weird
That's just,

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.950
for me, as your Mum,I don't know,

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.040
you won't know how it feels but,

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.610
I just want to tell the world,

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.100
I want to go out, outside, and shout,

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:36.933
(laughs)

00:09:36.933 --> 00:09:38.197
down my street,

00:09:38.197 --> 00:09:40.709
"This is my daughter, look look!".

00:09:40.709 --> 00:09:43.380
I do, I really seriously do.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:44.260
- Yeah.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:48.129
- You've done amazingly,
I'm so proud of you Es.

00:09:48.129 --> 00:09:48.962
- Aw Mum!

